<section class="section scroll-mt-16" aria-labelledby="mt5-heading">
  <div class="container-page">
    <div class="grid items-start gap-12 lg:grid-cols-2">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">MT5 integration</p>
        <h2 id="mt5-heading" class="heading-2 mt-2">Two layers, clearly separated</h2>
        <p class="body mt-4">
          The platform never touches your broker directly. It holds your strategy
          configuration and your account state; your MT5 Expert Advisor reads that
          configuration and does the trading.
        </p>
        <p class="body mt-4">
          That separation means your credentials and your funds stay where they already
          are — with your broker, in your own terminal.
        </p>
        <p class="caption mt-6">
          MT5 connectivity is not available yet. The platform is being built so it can be
          added without changing how your strategy is configured.
        </p>
      </div>

